module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.StupidTruncationTriangle
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CompleteGlobalSection
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Completion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.IdealOfGlobalSections

/-!
# The completion map is invertible on a derived-complete object

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪`. The completion
functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is `K ↦ K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)`, and the completion map
`K ⟶ K^∧` is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit`. This file proves clause 2 of the
section "What remains for Tag 099B" of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/Completion.lean`: the
completion map is invertible as soon as `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K) = 0` for every non-empty
`S ⊆ {1, …, r}`, and therefore whenever `K` is derived complete along a sheaf of ideals
containing the restrictions of the generators.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_pi`: the derived internal Hom into `K`
  out of a *finite product* vanishes as soon as it vanishes out of each factor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shift` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shiftNat`: that vanishing
  descends along a shift.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_singleFunctor_awayModule`: the vanishing
  at `𝒪_g` placed in an arbitrary non-negative degree, from `MemVanishingIdeal`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_one`: the vanishing out of
  the kernel `Č(f)^{≥1}` of the augmentation, by the induction on the stupid filtration.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal`:
  **the completion map `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible** when `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K) = 0` for every
  non-empty `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete`: the same with
  the hypothesis in the form of [Stacks, Tag 0999], which is the hypothesis `hη` of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_of_mem`:
  [Stacks, Tag 099B] for the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` with that hypothesis
  discharged, so reduced to the two others — derived completeness of every `K^∧` and
  idempotence of the unit. Those are clauses 1 and 3 of `Completion.lean`'s "The three clauses
  for Tag 099B"; both are proved in the neighbouring `CompletionIdempotent.lean`, which carries
  the tag's attribute on the hypothesis-free form, so the attribute is not attached here.
* `RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections` and
  `RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections_of_completion`: the two
  previous results at `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)`, where the membership hypothesis is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections` and so costs nothing.

## Implementation notes

**The degree-`p` term of `Č(f)` is a categorical product, not an iterated biproduct.** It is
`CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.term`, the product `∏_{S} 𝒪_{f_S}` over the subtype
`CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.Idx r p` of subsets of cardinality `p`. So the reduction of the
induction's hypothesis at that term to its factors is not a finite iteration of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_biprod` but `isZero_derivedSheafHom_pi`
below, which is that lemma's indexed form and is proved not by induction on the index type but
from additivity: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.additive_derivedSheafHom_flip_obj` makes
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(-, K)` an additive functor `D(𝒪)ᵒᵖ ⥤ D(𝒪)`, hence one preserving finite products,
and `op (∏ᶜ A)` *is* a finite product in `D(𝒪)ᵒᵖ` because a finite product in an additive
category is also a coproduct (`CategoryTheory.Limits.opCoproductIsoProduct` after
`biproduct.isoProduct` and `biproduct.isoCoproduct`). The finite products of `D(𝒪)` and of
`D(𝒪)ᵒᵖ` are those of any pretriangulated category.

**The degrees have to be moved.** `MemVanishingIdeal` is the vanishing at `𝒪_g` placed in degree
*zero*, while the induction supplies its terms in degree `p`. The two are compared by
`CategoryTheory.SingleFunctors.shiftIso`, which identifies `((single p).obj M)⟦p⟧` with
`(single 0).obj M`, together with `isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shiftNat`. The latter is
*not* a `CategoryTheory.Functor.CommShift` for the derived internal Hom — none exists in this
development, as recorded in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedHomTriangulated.lean` — but the
vanishing alone, read off the rotated contractible triangle `A ⟶ 0 ⟶ A⟦1⟧` through
[Stacks, Tag 08JC].

**From the kernel of the augmentation to the unit.** The filtration triangle at `p = 0`,
`StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGETriangle Č 0`, has vertices
`Č^{≥1}`, `Č^{≥0}` and `Č⁰[0]`; derived internal Hom into `K` turns it into a distinguished
triangle whose third vertex is `R𝑆heafHom(Č^{≥1}, K) = 0`, so its first morphism — the one
induced by `StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGEπ Č 0` — is invertible. The augmentation
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.cechAugmentation` is that projection composed with two
isomorphisms: `Č^{≥0} ≅ Č`, because `Č` vanishes in negative degrees, and `Č⁰ ≅ 𝒪`, because the
degree-zero index type is a singleton and `f_∅ = 1`. That is
`ιStupidTrunc_comp_cechAugmentation` below, checked in degree zero by
`HomologicalComplex.to_single_hom_ext`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0997](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0997)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite
open HomologicalComplex ComplexShape

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Vanishing

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))

/-- The vanishing of the derived internal Hom into `K` depends on its source only through its
isomorphism class. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso
    {A B : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (e : A ≅ B)
    (h : IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op A)).obj K)) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op B)).obj K) :=
  h.of_iso (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).mapIso e.op).app K)

/-- **Vanishing of the derived internal Hom into `K` is stable under finite products in the
source.** This is the indexed form of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_biprod`, and it is what reduces the
hypothesis of the stupid-filtration induction at a term of the Čech complex to its factors.

The functor `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(-, K) : D(𝒪)ᵒᵖ ⥤ D(𝒪)` is additive, so it preserves finite products;
and `op (∏ᶜ A)` is the product of the `op (A i)` in `D(𝒪)ᵒᵖ` because a finite product in an
additive category is also a coproduct. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_pi {ι : Type} [Finite ι]
    (A : ι → DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (hA : ∀ i, IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (A i))).obj K)) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (∏ᶜ A))).obj K) := by
  cases nonempty_fintype ι
  set H := (derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K with hH
  have e : (op (∏ᶜ A) :
        (DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))ᵒᵖ) ≅
      ∏ᶜ fun i ↦ op (A i) :=
    ((biproduct.isoCoproduct A).symm ≪≫ biproduct.isoProduct A).op ≪≫
      opCoproductIsoProduct A
  have hpi : IsZero (∏ᶜ fun i ↦ H.obj (op (A i))) := by
    rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
    exact Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun i ↦ (hA i).eq_of_tgt _ _
  exact hpi.of_iso (H.mapIso e ≪≫ PreservesProduct.iso H fun i ↦ op (A i))

/-- **The vanishing of the derived internal Hom into `K` descends along a shift.** If it vanishes
at `A⟦1⟧` then it vanishes at `A`: the rotated contractible triangle `A ⟶ 0 ⟶ A⟦1⟧` is
distinguished, and [Stacks, Tag 08JC] in the contravariant variable turns it into a distinguished
triangle with vertices `R𝑆heafHom(A⟦1⟧, K)`, `R𝑆heafHom(0, K)` and `R𝑆heafHom(A, K)`. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shift
    (A : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (h : IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (A⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧))).obj K)) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op A)).obj K) := by
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := exists_distinguished_derivedSheafHom X K (contractibleTriangle A).rotate
    (rot_of_distTriang _ (contractible_distinguished A))
  refine Triangle.isZero₃_of_isZero₁₂ _ hδ h ?_
  exact ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map_isZero
    (IsZero.op (isZero_zero
      (DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))))

/-- The vanishing of the derived internal Hom into `K` descends along a shift by a natural
number, by iterating `isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shift`. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shiftNat
    (A : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) (n : ℕ)
    (h : IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (A⟦(n : ℤ)⟧))).obj K)) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op A)).obj K) := by
  induction n generalizing A with
  | zero =>
      rw [show ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (0 : ℤ) from by norm_num] at h
      exact isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso X K
        ((shiftFunctorZero
          (DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
          ℤ).app A) h
  | succ n ih =>
      rw [show ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = (n : ℤ) + 1 from by push_cast; ring] at h
      refine ih A (isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shift X K (A⟦(n : ℤ)⟧) ?_)
      exact isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso X K
        ((shiftFunctorAdd'
          (DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
          (n : ℤ) 1 ((n : ℤ) + 1) rfl).app A) h

end Vanishing

section Cech

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- A term of the extended alternating Čech complex whose index type is empty is zero: it is an
empty product. -/
theorem isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_isEmpty {p : ℤ}
    (hp : IsEmpty (AlternatingCech.Idx r p)) :
    IsZero ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).X p) := by
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
  exact Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun b ↦ hp.elim b

/-- **The extended alternating Čech complex is bounded.** Its index type in degree `p` is the
subsets of `Fin r` of cardinality `p`, which is empty unless `0 ≤ p ≤ r`; so its non-zero terms
lie in `[0, r]`. This is the hypothesis `hK` of the stupid-filtration induction. -/
theorem finite_support_extendedAlternatingCech :
    {i : ℤ | ¬ IsZero ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).X i)}.Finite := by
  refine (Set.finite_Icc (0 : ℤ) r).subset fun i hi ↦ ?_
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hi
  refine Set.mem_Icc.2 ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · by_contra hlt
    exact hi (isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_neg X f (by omega))
  · by_contra hlt
    exact hi (isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_isEmpty X f
      (AlternatingCech.isEmpty_idx_of_lt (by omega)))

/-- The inclusion `Č(f)^{≥0} ⟶ Č(f)` is an isomorphism: the Čech complex vanishes in negative
degrees, so the truncation discards nothing. -/
theorem isIso_ιStupidTrunc_extendedAlternatingCech :
    IsIso ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc (embeddingUpIntGE 0)) := by
  have h : ∀ n, IsIso (((extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc
      (embeddingUpIntGE 0)).f n) := by
    intro n
    by_cases hn : (0 : ℤ) ≤ n
    · rw [StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.ιStupidTruncGE_f _ 0 n hn]
      infer_instance
    · exact IsZero.isIso
        (CochainComplex.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE
          ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).stupidTrunc (embeddingUpIntGE 0)) 0 n (by omega))
        (isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_neg X f (by omega)) _
  exact HomologicalComplex.Hom.isIso_of_components _

/-- **The degree-zero term of the Čech complex is `𝒪`.** The index type in degree zero is a
singleton, so the projection onto its unique factor is an isomorphism, and inverting
`f_∅ = 1` changes nothing. -/
theorem isIso_cechAugmentationZero : IsIso (cechAugmentationZero X f) := by
  have hπ : IsIso (Pi.π
      (fun S : AlternatingCech.Idx r 0 ↦ awayModule X (prodGlobalSection f S.1)) default) :=
    isIso_fan_proj_of_isZero (productIsProduct _) default
      fun a ha ↦ absurd (Subsingleton.elim a default) ha
  rw [cechAugmentationZero]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' hπ inferInstance

/-- **The augmentation is the projection onto the bottom term of the stupid filtration.** The
inclusion `Č(f)^{≥0} ⟶ Č(f)` followed by the augmentation `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]` is the projection
`Č(f)^{≥0} ⟶ Č(f)⁰[0]` followed by the identification of `Č(f)⁰` with `𝒪`. Both sides land in a
single complex, so the identity is checked in degree zero. -/
theorem ιStupidTrunc_comp_cechAugmentation :
    (extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc (embeddingUpIntGE 0) ≫ cechAugmentation X f =
      StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGEπ (extendedAlternatingCech X f) 0 ≫
        (single (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (up ℤ) 0).map
          (cechAugmentationZero X f) := by
  refine to_single_hom_ext ?_
  rw [HomologicalComplex.comp_f, HomologicalComplex.comp_f,
    StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.ιStupidTruncGE_f _ 0 0 le_rfl, cechAugmentation_f_zero,
    StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGEπ_f, HomologicalComplex.single_map_f_self]
  simp

end Cech

section Main

attribute [local instance] linearCatCenterRingSheaf
  isMulCommutative_over overCatCenterLinear
  overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits overFunctor_preservesFiniteColimits
  hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_over hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))

/-- **`MemVanishingIdeal` in an arbitrary non-negative degree.** If
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_g, K) = 0` with `𝒪_g` in degree zero, the same holds with `𝒪_g` placed in any
degree `p ≥ 0`: the shift identification of the single functors moves `(single p).obj 𝒪_g` to
`(single 0).obj 𝒪_g`, and the vanishing descends along a shift. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_singleFunctor_awayModule
    (h : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) {p : ℤ} (hp : 0 ≤ p)
    (hh : MemVanishingIdeal X K h) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj
      (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) p).obj
          (awayModule X h)))).obj K) := by
  refine isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_isZero_shiftNat X K _ p.toNat ?_
  rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg hp]
  exact isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso X K
    (((DerivedCategory.singleFunctors
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).shiftIso p 0 p
        (add_zero p)).app (awayModule X h)).symm hh

/-- **The derived internal Hom out of the kernel of the augmentation vanishes.** If
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K) = 0` for every non-empty `S`, then `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥1}, K) = 0`.

This is the induction on the stupid filtration of the bounded complex `Č(f)` run from the cut
`a = 1`: the extension step is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_obj₂_of_distTriang`, and the hypothesis at
the term `Č(f)ⁱ` with `i ≥ 1` is `isZero_derivedSheafHom_pi` over the subsets of cardinality
`i`, each of which is non-empty. -/
theorem isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_one
    (hv : ∀ S : Finset (Fin r), S.Nonempty → MemVanishingIdeal X K (prodGlobalSection f S)) :
    IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
      ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).stupidTrunc (embeddingUpIntGE 1))))).obj K) := by
  refine Stacks.DerivedCategory.BoundedInduction.property_of_bounded_complex_stupidTruncGE
    (fun A ↦ IsZero (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op A)).obj K))
    (fun e hA ↦ isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso X K e hA)
    (fun A hA ↦ ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map_isZero hA.op)
    (fun T hT h₁ h₃ ↦ isZero_derivedSheafHom_obj₂_of_distTriang X K T hT h₁ h₃)
    (extendedAlternatingCech X f) (finite_support_extendedAlternatingCech X f) 1
    fun i hi ↦ ?_
  refine isZero_derivedSheafHom_of_iso X K
    (PreservesProduct.iso
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) i)
      (fun S : AlternatingCech.Idx r i ↦ awayModule X (prodGlobalSection f S.1))).symm ?_
  refine isZero_derivedSheafHom_pi X K _ fun S ↦ ?_
  refine isZero_derivedSheafHom_singleFunctor_awayModule X K _ (by omega) ?_
  refine hv S.1 (Finset.card_pos.1 ?_)
  have := S.2
  omega

/-- **The augmentation induces an isomorphism on derived internal Hom into `K`.** The derived
internal Hom into `K` of the filtration triangle `Č(f)^{≥1} ⟶ Č(f)^{≥0} ⟶ Č(f)⁰[0]` is
distinguished with third vertex `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥1}, K) = 0`, so the map it induces from
`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)⁰[0], K)` is invertible; and the augmentation is the projection to `Č(f)⁰[0]`
composed with the two isomorphisms `Č(f)^{≥0} ≅ Č(f)` and `Č(f)⁰ ≅ 𝒪`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafHom_map_cechAugmentation
    (hv : ∀ S : Finset (Fin r), S.Nonempty → MemVanishingIdeal X K (prodGlobalSection f S)) :
    IsIso (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)).op) := by
  -- The filtration triangle at `p = 0`, pushed through the derived internal Hom.
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := exists_distinguished_derivedSheafHom X K
    (StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGETriangle (extendedAlternatingCech X f) 0)
    (StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGETriangle_distinguished
      (extendedAlternatingCech X f) 0)
  have hπ : IsIso (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map (StacksDraft.StupidTruncation.stupidTruncGEπ
        (extendedAlternatingCech X f) 0)).op) :=
    (Triangle.isZero₃_iff_isIso₁ _ hδ).1 (isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_one X f K hv)
  -- The two isomorphisms through which the augmentation factors.
  have hι : IsIso ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc (embeddingUpIntGE 0)) :=
    isIso_ιStupidTrunc_extendedAlternatingCech X f
  have hz : IsIso (cechAugmentationZero X f) := isIso_cechAugmentationZero X f
  have h2 : IsIso (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc
        (embeddingUpIntGE 0) ≫ cechAugmentation X f)).op) := by
    rw [ιStupidTrunc_comp_cechAugmentation X f]
    simp only [Functor.map_comp, op_comp]
    infer_instance
  rw [Functor.map_comp, op_comp, Functor.map_comp] at h2
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_right _
    (((derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj K).map
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map ((extendedAlternatingCech X f).ιStupidTrunc
        (embeddingUpIntGE 0))).op)

/-- **The completion map `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible.** If `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K) = 0` for every
non-empty subset `S` of `{1, …, r}`, then `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit` is an
isomorphism at `K`.

This is clause 2 of the section "What remains for Tag 099B" of `Completion.lean`: the completion
map is the identification `K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)` followed by the map the augmentation induces,
and that map is invertible by `isIso_derivedSheafHom_map_cechAugmentation`. -/
theorem isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal
    (hv : ∀ S : Finset (Fin r), S.Nonempty → MemVanishingIdeal X K (prodGlobalSection f S)) :
    IsIso ((completionUnit X f).app K) := by
  have haug := isIso_derivedSheafHom_map_cechAugmentation X f K hv
  rw [completionUnit_app]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' inferInstance haug

/-- **The hypothesis `hη` of [Stacks, Tag 099F], discharged.** If `K` is derived complete along a
sheaf of ideals `ℐ` all of whose slices contain the restrictions of the generators
`f_1, …, f_r`, then the completion map `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible.

This composes `isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_of_isDerivedComplete`, which
supplies the vanishing at every non-empty subproduct. -/
theorem isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete
    [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hI : ∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.C),
      globalSectionVal (f i) (op U) ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op U))
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I K) :
    IsIso ((completionUnit X f).app K) :=
  isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal X f K fun _ hS ↦
    memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_of_isDerivedComplete X K f I hI hK hS

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099B] for the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, with the hypothesis
`hη` discharged.** `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion`
asks for three properties of the Čech candidate `(Φ, η)`; the second of them, invertibility of
`K ⟶ K^∧` on a derived-complete `K`, is `isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete` above, so
only the first and the third remain.

The tag's attribute is *not* attached here, because its carrier is the hypothesis-free form in
the neighbouring `CompletionIdempotent.lean`. The first hypothesis `hΦ`, derived completeness of
every `K^∧`, is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_completionFunctor` there; the
third, the idempotence `Φ η_K = η_{Φ K}` which the two-object counterexample of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletion.lean` shows cannot be dropped,
is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor_map_completionUnit_app` there, which assumes
`hΦ` and nothing else. -/
theorem isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_of_mem
    [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    (hI : ∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.C),
      globalSectionVal (f i) (op U) ∈ I.toSubmodule.obj (op U))
    (hΦ : ∀ L, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I ((completionFunctor X f).obj L))
    (hcomm : ∀ L, (completionFunctor X f).map ((completionUnit X f).app L) =
      (completionUnit X f).app ((completionFunctor X f).obj L)) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I)).IsRightAdjoint :=
  isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion X f I hΦ
    (fun L hL ↦ isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete X f L I hI hL) hcomm

/-- **`hη` at the ideal sheaf the construction actually uses.** For
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` the membership hypothesis of
`isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections`, so the completion map
is invertible on every object derived complete along `ℐ` with no side condition at all. -/
theorem isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections
    [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K) :
    IsIso ((completionUnit X f).app K) :=
  isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete X f K (idealOfGlobalSections X f)
    (fun i U ↦ globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections X f i (op U)) hK

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099B] for `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)`, reduced to clauses 1 and 3.** The inclusion of
the objects of `D(𝒪)` derived complete along the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` has a
left adjoint as soon as every completion `K^∧` is derived complete along `ℐ` and the completion
functor carries the unit to the unit.

Together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections` of
`IdealOfGlobalSections.lean` this is the whole of the source's proof *except* those two
properties of `(Φ, η)`. Both are discharged in `CompletionIdempotent.lean`, which carries the
tag's attribute on the resulting
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections`. -/
theorem isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections_of_completion
    [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (hΦ : ∀ L, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f)
      ((completionFunctor X f).obj L))
    (hcomm : ∀ L, (completionFunctor X f).map ((completionUnit X f).app L) =
      (completionUnit X f).app ((completionFunctor X f).obj L)) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι
      (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f))).IsRightAdjoint :=
  isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_of_mem X f (idealOfGlobalSections X f)
    (fun i U ↦ globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections X f i (op U)) hΦ hcomm

end Main

